==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first requirement, focus on picking up [[Research Capsules]] and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Capsule count increases the further you descend, so you can earn more {{II|Ichor|name=true}}.
*For the second requirement, have a Distractor [[Toon]] bring {{CI|Twisted Pebble|name=true}} to the [[Elevator]] to you so you can get aggro. Playing as {{CI|Rodger|name=true}} also helps getting Research faster because of his Passive [[Ability]]. This will be easier if Twisted Pebble is on the [[Daily Twisted Board]].
*For the third requirement, play as {{CI|Toodles|name=true}} and try to complete her [[Mastery]] Quests by going on multiple runs. It is recommended to go on an organized Run or do specific quests in certain runs.

==Strategies==
If you like zooming around the place, Pebble is the one for you. Having the highest [[Movement Speed]] in the game (5{{Star}}) and high [[Stamina]] (4 Stars), Pebble possesses both high survivability and the ability to distract Twisteds proficiently. It is not recommended to focus on extraction with this [[Toon]] as his [[Extraction Speed]] is significantly lower than other Toons, although having a 3 Star [[Skill Check]] makes it a little more bearable.

Pebble is an ideal distractor due to his Movement Speed and [[Stamina]], but if you are in a difficult situation, you are more likely to get hit if you are not careful. If you are distracting multiple {{Type|Main}} Twisteds, you will need to sprint if {{CI|Twisted Vee|name=true}} inflicts the {{Debuff|Slow|II}} [[Debuff]], {{CI|Twisted Pebble|name=true}}, {{CI|Twisted Glisten|name=true}} when enraged; etc. It is recommended to have an {{CI|Astro|name=true}} by your side when distracting a difficult combination of Twisteds and use his Active Ability to help regenerate your Stamina faster. Only sprint if a fast Twisted catches up to you, even if you are turning corners, do not sprint unless they're about to hit you. You should not have other Twisteds that are significantly slower than others on you when distracting, as they may lose line of sight of you and you will have to go out of your way to regather them, which may lead to some hits or they could turn the other way and hit you. Stay in one area away from [[Machines]] or Items so Twisted Pebble will not lose aggro on you and chase after any other Toons who pass through the area where you are distracting.

Pebble's Active Ability is a very useful tool while distracting Twisteds. '''Speak!''' is able to help save other Toons being chased by Twisteds by forcing the Twisteds to chase you instead. It alerts Twisteds to your location (like a failed Skill Check; most must be nearby to notice) and also lowers your Stealth by 50 units. This means that to steal aggro from other players you will still need to be in the Twisted's detection range, so be careful not to use it from too far behind if chasing a Twisted. If you are distracting in a narrow area and see that a Toon with lower or equal Stealth is attempting to get through the area, consider using '''Speak!''' to reduce the risk. '''Speak!''' is most useful when in a sticky situation while distracting, allowing for you to take the aggro off of most Toons and safely allow them to pass. Another alternative to '''Speak!''' could be collecting {{II|Air Horn|name=true}}s that you find around the map, as they are a great replacement for the Ability if it not able to be used at the moment.

Pebble's Passive Ability can assist you with finding Items quicker. '''Fetch!''', like the name says, assists you with finding Items scattered around the floor by highlighting them, allowing you to find useful Items such as healing or speed Items, the former of which should be pointed out to teammates if unneeded. '''Fetch!''' is also great if you're searching for [[Research Capsules]] to grind [[Ichor]] or [[Research]], but be careful to continue paying attention to your surroundings, as '''Fetch!''' will still highlight the fake {{CI|Twisted Rodger|name=true}} capsule.

Pebble is an excellent pick for grinding [[Event]] [[Currencies]]/Research due to high mobility and the ability to detect Event Items and capsules/attract Twisted aggro easily. With the right Trinkets, he can also make a good extractor or solo Toon, making up for any deficits with near-unmatched speed. It can help to have {{CI|Shelly|name=true}} or {{CI|Brusha|name=true}} on your team to heat up your extraction, especially when combined with Trinkets and Items. You can also focus on taking care of Treadmill Machines or assisting with Duo Machines, covering possible weak spots of other extractors, or simply to get Floors completed faster overall. When extracting as Pebble, you should still try to support your team using your Abilities and Stats; use your mobility to gather Twisteds for a distractor (if there is one) and to protect slower teammates; use the bark to alert Twisteds away from a Machine, the Elevator, or a vulnerable teammate without having to directly take aggro; use the bark to save low Stealth teammates when a distractor or other Toons can't; use the Item highlight to lead {{CI|Sprout|name=true}} or {{CI|Ginger|name=true}} to {{Tape|name=true}}, lead {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}} or injured teammates to healing Items, lead vulnerable teammates to survival Items like {{II|Smoke Bomb|name=false|plural=a}}, or just bring yourself to find Items to help in survival or extracting.

Overall, Pebble is a great distractor Toon, a good support, and also has somewhat of a capacity to be an extractor, though if you aren't aware of your surroundings, he won't be good at any of these.

===Trinket Combinations===
{{Preference}}
For specific [[Trinket]] recommendations, here are some possible combinations:

====Distraction====
*'''{{TI|Dog Plush|name=true}}/Options'''
**This Trinket alone allows Pebble to outwalk anything besides {{CI|Twisted Pebble|name=true}}, {{CI|Twisted Glisten|name=true}} when enraged, {{CI|Twisted Coal|name=true}} when a [[Blackout]] is present, and some others {{Small|(22 walk speed)}}. Keep in mind that Dog Plush will make Pebble much faster than slower Twisteds such as {{CI|Twisted Shrimpo|name=true}}, which would make him lose them more easily. Here are some options to pair Dog Plush with:
***'''{{TI|Speedy Shoes|name=true}}''', to further improve walk speed, more preferable for those new to distracting as Pebble {{Small|(23.1 walk speed)}};
***'''{{TI|Clown Horn|name=true}}/{{TI|Ribbon Spool|name=true}}''', to also out-walk before Panic Mode Twisted Glisten, Twisted Pebble, and Twisted Vee when you are inflicted with the {{Debuff|Slow|II}} [[Debuff]] when active {{Small|(24.2 walk/33 run speed)}};
****Do note this Trinket combo is best used when duo-distracting with another player.
***'''{{TI|Vanity Mirror|name=true}}''', to out-run almost all Twisteds during [[Panic Mode]] while active {{Small|(39 run speed)}};
***'''{{TI|Train Whistle|name=true}}''', to completely nullify the {{Debuff|Slow|}} Debuff, making {{CI|Twisted Vee|name=true}} significantly easier to distract, and [[Ichor Leaks]] much easier to distract in;
***'''{{TI|Scrapbook|name=true}}''', to be able to distract without other 3{{Star}} [[Stealth]] Toons taking aggro off you;
****Only use this Trinket combo if most of the players in your run have 3 Star [[Stealth]].
***'''{{TI|Megaphone|name=true}}''', to give access to what is essentially Pebble's Active Ability more easily;
****Only use these Trinket combinations if your teammates are unorganized or have 3 Star and below [[Stealth]].
***Any of the Trinkets in the '''Extraction Section''', to help with Floor progression; etc.

====Extraction====
*'''{{TI|Magnifying Glass|name=true}}/Options'''
**This Trinket allows Pebble to take full advantage over his 1{{Star}} [[Extraction Speed]] {{Small|(0.75 extraction speed)}} and 3 Star [[Skill Check]] {{Small|(100.5 skill check size)}}. Here are some options to pair Magnifying Glass with:
***'''{{TI|Vee's Remote|name=true}}''', to allow for quicker Floor progression, especially if teammates also carry Vee's Remote;
***'''{{TI|Participation Award|name=true}}''', to speed up [[Machine]] completion by maximizing Skill Check extraction {{Small|(29.8 avg/27.21 with Tech Savvy)}};
***Any Trinkets listed in the '''Distraction''' section, to help with survival.

====Ability====
*'''{{TI|Ghost Snakes In A Can|name=true}}''', to reduce {{AI|Pebble|name=true}}'s [[Ability|Abilit]]<nowiki/>[[Ability|y]] cooldown {{Small|(55s)}}.
**'''{{TI|Sweet Charm|name=true}}''', to further reduce '''Speak!'''<nowiki/>'s cooldown, though only by a medium amount as the Trinket works with percentages {{Small|(50.2s)}}.

'''Note: It is NOT recommended to use Trinkets that highlight Items such as {{TI|Memory Locket|name=true}}, {{TI|Research Map|name=true}}, and {{Type|Common}} Event Trinkets, as Pebble can already see Items with his Passive Ability.'''

