==Trivia==
*Pebble's [[Toon Handler]] is {{CI|Devan Reed|name=true}}, with the latter also being {{CI|Dandy|name=true}}'s Toon Handler.
*Pebble is [[Dandy]]'s pet rock. <ref>[[Dandy#Quotes|"Hey, that's my pet rock! Take good care of him will ya?"]]</ref>
**The clover-like markings on his cheeks likely represent Dandy in some way, subtly restating that Pebble is Dandy's pet rock.
**Moreover, in his {{Skin|Loyal Bud}} [[Skin]], Pebble sports a flower bud on his back with the colors of the petals mirroring Dandy's, further highlighting that Pebble is Dandy's pet rock.
***The name of the skin itself is a clever pun: "bud" refers not only to the flower bud. but by playing on the word "buddy", it once again reiterates the fact he is Dandy's pet rock.
**His owner, {{CI|Dyle|name=true}}, and {{CI|Gourdy|name=true}}'s [[Gossips]] about Pebble and his full name reaffirm that Pebble is Dandy's pet rock.
*Pebble met [[Dandy]] in 8/24/1987, which implies Pebble was created before that date.
*Pebble and {{CI|Coal|name=true}} are confirmed to be friends, as seen by the fact she has to survive 5 rounds with Pebble for her [[Mastery]], and {{CI|Bobette}}[[Bobette|her owner]] directly confirms in her gossip that she and him are friends.
*His name is used to describe a small rock, which is exactly what he is. His design may be a pun on rockhounding, a slang term for {{wp|amateur geology}}.
*Pebble is designation M-001 with the '''M''' standing most likely for {{Type|Main}}. The -001 means he was the first Main Character to be created by [[Delilah]], with him being made sometime before the 24th of August 1987, and was the second [[Toon]] overall to be created after [[Dandy]].
*Pebble, {{CI|Waxwell|name=true}}, and {{CI|Bassie|name=true}} are the only Toons with 5{{Star}} [[Movement Speed]] (though {{CI|Razzle|name=true}} can reach the equivalent on odd Floors, and {{CI|Looey|name=true}} can roughly reach their speed or even outspeed all of them when missing any {{Heart}}). 
**However, Pebble, Waxwell and Bassie are the only Toons to consistently have this speed, as the Twin Masks and Looey are situational.
***Pebble is the only one of the three to:
****Be in the game on release.
****Release unoptimized.
****Not be humanoid.
****Have 1 Star [[Extraction Speed]]
****Have any 3 Star [[Stat]] at all.
****Have [[Mastery]] requiring [[Twisteds]] in some way.
****Not have Mastery requiring Machines in any regard.
****Not have Mastery requiring using any [[Items]].
*Pebble was the only [[Toon]] with a "Reach [[Floor]]" [[Mastery]] requirement before [[Bobette]], [[Bassie]], {{CI|Flutter|name=true}}, and {{CI|Flyte|name=true}} were added, making their Mastery some of the most difficult to complete.
*Pebble's [[Star-Time]] [[Skin]] has a bigger tail than any of his other skin models. This was likely intentional to fit all the stickers on it.
*Pebble is the first [[Toon]] to have his [[Abilities]] completely scrapped and changed, the second being {{CI|Soulvester|name=true}}. During the same update, his [[Mastery]] was also altered, causing anyone who had completed the old requirement to lose it and those with the completed Mastery to revert to 5/6 progress on him and lose the icon sparkles.
**However, they still retained access to the {{Skin|Vintage}} [[Skin]]. The new requirement is 'Encounter 80 [[Twisteds]]'.
**Pebble's old Active Ability has been reworked into [[Coal]]'s Active Ability.
***Coal's ability highlights for everyone instead of just herself.
**Pebble's old Passive Ability ('''Survival Instincts''') increased his stealth and stamina by 25% whenever he was on one {{Heart}}.
*If you looked inside Pebble, you would see a 3D modeled tongue, which would've been used for animations but ended up being unused (all the way to [[Changelog|v0.6.4]]). Two of Pebble's [[Skins]], {{Skin|Loyal Bud}} and {{Skin|Thorned Geode}}, had a different colored tongue, except for his [[Star-Time]] Skin, while his {{Skin|Vintage}} Skin had a colored one. The tongue was removed in v0.7.1, but {{CI|Twisted Pebble|name=true}} retains his.
*All of the dog characters (him, [[Coal]], and {{CI|Eclipse|name=true}}) have staring problems. Pebble's in particular are directly pointed out by {{CI|Sprout|name=true}} and {{CI|Ribecca|name=true}}, though the latter is significantly unluckier due to being made of bones.
*[[Twisteds]] with 9999 hearing radius, like {{CI|Twisted Vee|name=true}}, are alerted to Pebble's {{AI|Pebble|name=true}} [[Ability]] from anywhere on the map.
*Pebble is stated directly to be a {{wp|Pet Rock}}.
*Excluding [[Holiday Toons|Event Main Characters]], Pebble is the cheapest {{Type|Main}} [[Toon]], costing 3750 [[Ichor]].
*When Pebble uses his Active [[Ability]], the sound will be lower pitched on the user's side, but normal-pitched when heard by another player.
*Pebble is one of the few [[Toons]] without typical hands (or lacking hands entirely).
*Pebble is the first [[Toon]] to have a visible nose.
*Pebble is the only base-game [[Main]] [[Toon]] that haven't appeared in any of the episode storyboards currently.
*Pebble used to be the only one with the most Skins in [[Changelog|v0.9.5]] and earlier, until he tied with {{CI|Yatta|name=true}} in v0.10.1, fell when v0.11.1 released, and then tied again with her, Razzle & Dazzle, and {{CI|Shelly|name=true}} in v0.14.10, before getting another Skin with Razzle & Dazzle.
*Pebble can perform a backflip, confirmed by [[Dandy]] in his gossip dialogue. At some point, he landed on his back akin to a turtle when he did a flip, but didn't mind his predicament despite being assisted by his owner anyway.
*If you used both {{II|Air Horn|name=true}} and '''Speak''' [[Ability]], Pebble would have '''-90.00''' [[Stealth]]. This gives him Stealth similar to {{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}}'s, only being -9 units away.
*Pebble's full name is "Pebble Dancifer Jr.". He is the only pet to inherit a last name from their owner.
*According to their dialogues, {{CI|Scraps|name=true}} and Pebble do not seem to like each other, likely referencing the classic rivalry between cats and dogs.
**Meanwhile, {{CI|Goob|name=true}} and Pebble are friendly towards each other, and Goob doesn't understand their feud.
***This could be due to Goob having a few dog-like qualities in behavior and personality, and maybe they can relate to each other.
*Pebble's stats are nearly identical to that of [[Razzle]]'s, only being 1{{Star}} higher in Stamina.
*Prior to the release of [[Sprout]], Pebble used to have the shortest [[Ability]] cooldown of any main, being 30 seconds. Due to his Ability rework, he's now tied with [[Astro]] and [[Shelly]] at 60 seconds.
*Pebble is one of the few [[Toons]] whose [[Ability]] ends with an exclamation mark.
*Pebble used to have 2 Star Skill Check, making him the second slowest extractor ([[Shrimpo]] being the slowest) before being bumped up to 3 Stars.
**This makes Pebble the only [[Main]] Toon to have 3 Star Skill Check.
**At that time, Pebble was still the second slowest extractor, until the [[2025 Easter Event]] update, when [[Bassie]] was added.
*Pebble's [[Ability]] is essentially that of a failed [[Machine]] Skill Check, as [[Twisteds]] play their failed Skill Check detection noise when you use it. However, it also lowers his [[Stealth]].
*Pebble is the second [[Main]] to have updated models and animations, the first being [[Bobette]].
**He is the first one to be from the base game and to originally not have one.
*In [[Changelog|v0.7.2]], Pebble got a remodel and new idle animation where he twirls around on the spot. [[Twisted Pebble]] got new animations as well.
*The "{{Skin|Served Eggy}}" [[Skin]] for Pebble was originally dark gray during development, but was changed to a dark orange when it released.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/970049062608961560/1369071169185124422</ref> That and "{{Skin|Extra Cheese}}" make Pebble the first non-Holiday {{Type|Main}} to have an Event-exclusive skin.
*Pebble was designed to be a slow extractor with extremely high survivability. The role of distractor was created by the community with the Dev team following along with an Ability change.
*Pebble is currently the shortest [[Toon]], roughly reaching most of the [[Toons]]' hips.
*When [[Yatta]] is hit, killed or completes a Machine within '''Fetch!'''<nowiki/>'s range, Pebble is able to see the [[Items]] moving as they spawn and scatter.
*Pebble and {{CI|Brightney|name=true}} are one of the first non-[[Shrimpo]] Toons to have 1 Star on a [[Stat]].
**He's also the first {{Type|Main}} to have 1 Star on a Statistic, the second being [[Bassie]] and the third being [[Gourdy]].
*Pebble, {{CI|Toodles|name=true}}, and [[Blot]] are one of the few [[Toons]] to be predominantly grayscale.
*Pebble is going to be the last Main Character to get their own themed map, if he ends up getting one.
*Pebble and [[Sprout]] are the second [[Toons]] to have both their normal and Twisted counterparts appear in the game's thumbnail, with [[Razzle & Dazzle]] and [[Blot]] being first, [[Shelly]] being third, fourth being [[Gourdy]], and fifth being [[Coal]].
*Pebble and [[Bassie]] need to travel more meters for their [[Masteries]] than the other [[Mains]].
**Pebble actually needs to travel the most, being 175,000, making him need the most meters to complete a Mastery as a Main Character and a [[Toon]] in general, with Bassie being the second (requiring 160,000, 15,000 meters less).
*Pebble is the second [[Toon]], alongside [[Sprout]], to have both themselves and their [[Twisted Pebble|Twisted counterpart]] be in a thumbnail, being the [[Changelog|v0.1.0]] and v0.14 thumbnails.
*Pebble is the first [[Toon]] to be featured in 2 separate thumbnails, being in [[Changelog|v0.11]] and v0.12, with [[Shrimpo]] being second, [[Toodles]] being third, [[Gigi]] and {{CI|Rodger|name=true}} being fourth, [[Bobette]] being fifth, and the sixth being the rest of the [[Christmas Toons]].
*Pebble is one of three [[Main Characters]] to be in the game on release, the other two being [[Astro]] and [[Vee]].
*There was a bug that affected Pebble, {{CI|Flutter|name=true}}, and [[Coal]], where they would say [[Soulvester]]'s [[Ability]] dialogue while wearing his mask during the [[Haunted Gala]] [[Floor Event]]. Pebble and Coal naturally shouldn't be able to talk English due to their dog-like behavior. so the bug was eventually fixed to prevent them from going out of character in [[Changelog|v0.29.5]].
